Z||000000||Seanh||03-31-2001||10:56 PM||||I am in the process of replaceing the pickup coil on the distributor. I have marked the position of the rotor, distributor, and removed it from the engine. I see somthing that isn't covered in the haynes manual. My distributor is a little difference (reman.) Anyway, I wish I had a picture but I dont. I see a star shaped metal peice attached to the shaft. It looks to me that it needs to be removed to reaplace the pick-up. I can't see how to remove it? There is also a larger peice that goes around it, mounted to the distributor iself and it has points going into the center, looks as if it meets the star shaped peice on the shaft. How the hell do you remove it, or what do I do to replace the pickup coil? Thanks. I need the car tomarrow before noon, so I need some quick help to replace this tonight. Thanks again||||reg||1
Z||000001||bubbajoexx||03-31-2001||11:10 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Seanh:<BR><B>I am in the process of replaceing the pickup coil on the distributor. I have marked the position of the rotor, distributor, and removed it from the engine. I see somthing that isn't covered in the haynes manual. My distributor is a little difference (reman.) Anyway, I wish I had a picture but I dont. I see a star shaped metal peice attached to the shaft. It looks to me that it needs to be removed to reaplace the pick-up. I can't see how to remove it? There is also a larger peice that goes around it, mounted to the distributor iself and it has points going into the center, looks as if it meets the star shaped peice on the shaft. How the hell do you remove it, or what do I do to replace the pickup coil? Thanks. I need the car tomarrow before noon, so I need some quick help to replace this tonight. Thanks again</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>remove the lower gear by removing the quench pin the pull the main shaft out of the dist. the remove the three screws on the indution coil and replace it with the new one and reinstall the main shaft and lower gear and you are done||||reg||1
Z||000002||Will||03-31-2001||11:18 PM||||I just read your other thread. I hope you're not following bad advice.<BR>Are you sure you need a new pickup coil? Did you check the strength of you spark before you did all this tearing down?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Seanh||04-01-2001||12:06 AM||||Ahhh. I figured it out.. I got it now. In the begining, I wasn't sure I needed a new one, but once I got it off, and used the "testing" procedure in the Haynes manual, I found it to apperently be bad according to their standards. It really wasn't much work, after rebuilding the top end of the engine, this was a peice of cake. I should have done it when I had the engine apart, but I didn't so now I'm paying.<P>P.S. I also needed to replace the O-ring on the distributor, so this wasn't to much out of the way. I reused the old o-ring on the rebuild, and it is leaking ever so slightly.||||reg||1
